summary:
Round 1's fixes do what they set out to do. A decided call a reshape re-sorts is demanded again (R1-10). An override's own disposition decides (R1-11). The plan approver is shown the record's files (R1-2). The unreachable mitigation fallbacks are gone, and the fix diff's own changes introduce no new correctness bug.

The findings are all places where the record and what an agent or reader is shown still disagree:
- a stray resolve entry beside an override stays in the approver's and the implementer's lists;
- the implementer and the plan dial still carry the shaper's files or words;
- a replan of a decided deferral is never seen;
- the result's deferred entry and a decided reply still read empty words or mention-only commits as nothing shipped.

The rest is stale prose (the standard's done rule, the schema comment, FILES_ASK beside the ask-rules block), one unpinned neighbour of R1-11, and two small refactors. No scheduled or queued work exists in this repository.

findings.description:
R1-7's fix changed two sentences to an absolute:
- the comment at 777-778: "The words are shown, at a stop and in the result, only beside a mitigation the record says ships";
- docs/running.md ("Whether a mitigation shipped"): "which are shown only beside a mitigation that ships".

The plan-dial stop does not keep it. `handoffResult` returns `deferredPlanned: outcome.shaped.deferred` (4681) with each entry's `mitigation` words as the shaper wrote them, whatever its `files` say. It returns `plan[].recommendation` the same way (4680).

Example:
- the shaper defers R1-1 with mitigation `a guard on the queue` and `files: []`, under `interrupt: plan`;
- `deferredPlanned[0].mitigation` is `a guard on the queue`;
- the same stop's `drafts[0]`, from `draftView` (3406-3408), is `ships: false, mitigation: ''`.

The skill is told to read `files` for a defer "whatever its words say" (skills/redline/SKILL.md:184). So the person is not misled through the skill's own reading, but the comment and the doc are untrue at this stop.

The test "a commit of the finding's own landed" is computed separately in three places:
- `own = named.filter((c) => ownCommit(c, f.id))` in `outcomesFor` (2937);
- `landed(id) = roundCommits.some((c) => ownCommit(c, id))` (4053);
- the warning's recomputed `roundCommits.filter((c) => ownCommit(c, d.item.id))` (4061).

`deferredEntry` (3388) and `draftView` (3406) read `outcome.commits.length`, which comes from the first, so they are not further copies. The candidate's count of five overstates.

The three agree today, since every commit that `ownCommit` accepts is in `named`. A later change to what counts as a deferral's own commit has to be made in each. `outcomes[id].commits.length` does not replace `landed` for every caller: `buys(finalOwn, ...)` also runs for a decided call a reshape re-sorted to defer, whose outcome lists commits that only mention it.
